Pugh, retiring Chairman;
Councillor Mrs. Underhay, Mayor of Eastbourne; the Countess of Kilmuir, EAW
President; Professor M. W.

Stewart, Founder Chairman, and past Chairman of
Scottish Council, was the guest speaker. Peterhead had a talk on First Aid by Nurse Mutch;
and an illustrated travel talk by Mrs. Walter Allen.

The AGM was held. Salisbury had a demonstration of flower arranging;
a filmshow by Mr. Bulmer, SEB; and the AGM was
held.

Neale,
AO, spoke on 'The Wise Consumer' Campaign. Yeovil had a talk by a policewoman from Taunton;
a hairdressing demonstration by Bernard of Mayfair;
and filmshows by the SEB. The AGM was held.
